# LeakSanitizer suppressions for MiNiFi C++ test runs.
# Wired into CTest via LSAN_OPTIONS in the add_test() override in cmake/BuildTests.cmake
# (only for MINIFI_ADVANCED_ASAN_BUILD builds).
#
# Syntax: `leak:<substring>` suppresses a leak if the substring matches any frame's
# (demangled) function name, source file, or module in the leak's stack trace.

# Extensions are loaded via dlopen() at startup and cannot be fully unloaded at exit
# (STB_GNU_UNIQUE symbols and third-party singletons such as RocksDB's Env::Default()
# keep the .so mapped -- see the comment in Extension::~Extension()). The LeakSanitizer
# in Clang 20 therefore reports the load-time global allocations of every loaded extension
# as leaks. In a running agent these are persistent process-lifetime globals, not true
# leaks, so we suppress the whole extension-loading path. Both frames below are present
# in every such leak; listing both is robust to one being inlined into the other.
leak:org::apache::nifi::minifi::core::extension::Extension::load
leak:org::apache::nifi::minifi::core::extension::ExtensionManager::ExtensionManager
